NNAAMMEE
     hhppttmmvv — HighPoint RocketRAID 182x device driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee hhppttmmvv

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           hptmv_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhppttmmvv driver provides support for HighPoint's RocketRAID 182x based
     RAID controller.

     These devices support ATA disk drives and provide RAID0 (striping), RAID1
     (mirroring), and RAID5 functionality.

HHAARRDDWWAARREE
     The hhppttmmvv driver supports the following ATA RAID controllers:

     ••   HighPoint's RocketRAID 182x series

NNOOTTEESS
     The hhppttmmvv driver only works on the i386 and amd64 platforms as it re‐
     quires a binary blob object from the manufacturer which they only supply
     for these platforms.  The hhppttmmvv driver does _n_o_t work on i386 with pae(4)
     enabled.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     kld(4), kldload(8), loader(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The hhppttmmvv device driver first appeared in FreeBSD 5.3.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
     The hhppttmmvv device driver was written by HighPoint Technologies, Inc., and
     ported to FreeBSD by Scott Long.  This manual page was written by David
     E. O'Brien.

BBUUGGSS
     The hhppttmmvv driver does not support manipulating the RAID from the OS,
     RAIDs need to be set up from the on-board BIOS.

